head.b:skin:
/*
  <Group description="Backgrounds">
    <Variable name="bg1" description="Fondo 1" type="color" default="#fff"/>
    <Variable name="bg2" description="Fondo 2" type="color" default="#0f172a"/>
  </Group>
*/
/* Demo */
* { margin: 0 }
body {
  background-color: #fff;
  padding: 2rem;
}

/*Test*/
.bg1 { background-color: $(bg1) }
.bg2 { background-color: $(bg2) }
[data-theme="dark"] { color: #fff }
[data-theme="dark"] .contrast::before { content: "true" }
[data-theme="light"] .contrast::before { content: "false" }

article { padding: 1rem; max-width: 500px; }

b:includable.b:comment:
Evaluates a color's brightness and exposes its contrast state.
@author zkreations
@param {Color} color - Color variable from data:skin.vars
@param {Number} [threshold=155] - Brightness limit to trigger the dark state (0-255)
@param {String} [attr="data-theme"] - Target attribute name to render
